From: EdgeFirst <noreply@edgefirst.ai>
Subject: [PATCH] neutron: call matmul() with the typed header

eIQ Neutron SDK 3.2.x declares

    NeutronError matmul(const NeutronMatmulHeader *info, const void *in,
                        int sizeIn, const void *out, int sizeOut, int idxSlot);

in place of the earlier form that took the header as a void pointer followed by
its size in bytes. NeutronMatmulHeader is the same sixteen packed 32-bit words
the provider already builds in m_header, so the call only changes type and
drops the size argument.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [targets the eIQ Neutron SDK that this layer republishes; NXP's onnxruntime still targets the older driver API]
---
diff -ru a/onnxruntime/core/providers/neutron/ops/matmul_integer.cc b/onnxruntime/core/providers/neutron/ops/matmul_integer.cc
--- a/onnxruntime/core/providers/neutron/ops/matmul_integer.cc	2026-10-20 06:21:10.625074785 +0000
+++ b/onnxruntime/core/providers/neutron/ops/matmul_integer.cc	2026-10-20 06:21:10.669076826 +0000
@@ -310,7 +310,7 @@
     clock_gettime(CLOCK_REALTIME, &t3);
 
     NeutronError ret = ENONE;
-    ret = matmul((const void *)m_header, 16*sizeof(uint32_t), (const void*)a_neutron, a_size, (const void*)y_neutron, y_size, m_handle);
+    ret = matmul((const NeutronMatmulHeader *)m_header, (const void*)a_neutron, a_size, (const void*)y_neutron, y_size, m_handle);
     if (ret != ENONE){
         return ORT_MAKE_STATUS(ONNXRUNTIME, FAIL, "matmul() error");
     }
diff -ru a/onnxruntime/core/providers/neutron/ops/matmul_integer_to_float.cc b/onnxruntime/core/providers/neutron/ops/matmul_integer_to_float.cc
--- a/onnxruntime/core/providers/neutron/ops/matmul_integer_to_float.cc	2026-10-20 06:21:10.629074970 +0000
+++ b/onnxruntime/core/providers/neutron/ops/matmul_integer_to_float.cc	2026-10-20 06:21:10.669076826 +0000
@@ -357,7 +357,7 @@
     clock_gettime(CLOCK_REALTIME, &t3);
 
     NeutronError ret = ENONE;
-    ret = matmul((const void *)m_header, 16*sizeof(uint32_t), (const void*)a_neutron, a_size, (const void*)y_neutron, y_size, m_handle);
+    ret = matmul((const NeutronMatmulHeader *)m_header, (const void*)a_neutron, a_size, (const void*)y_neutron, y_size, m_handle);
     if (ret != ENONE){
         return ORT_MAKE_STATUS(ONNXRUNTIME, FAIL, "matmul() error");
     }
